WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:12.275
You're pretty!

2
00:00:12.276 --> 00:00:16.632
You're pretty!

3
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:21.377
Who are you?

4
00:00:21.378 --> 00:00:25.165
I'm a monarch butterfly.

5
00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:30.461
Butterflies are insects.

6
00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:33.281
Where do you live?

7
00:00:33.282 --> 00:00:37.812
We stay near a plant called milkweed.

8
00:00:37.813 --> 00:00:43.772
We live in North America in spring and summer.

9
00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:48.455
In the fall we fly away.

10
00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:52.112
Oh! Where do you go?

11
00:00:52.113 --> 00:00:58.971
Monarch butterflies usually fly to Mexico.

12
00:00:58.972 --> 00:01:03.773
It's much warmer there.

13
00:01:03.774 --> 00:01:06.740
That's a long trip!

14
00:01:06.741 --> 00:01:11.736
Yes. We fly thousands of kilometers.

15
00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:16.141
I've never made the trip before.

16
00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:20.744
But I'll know where to go.

17
00:01:20.745 --> 00:01:24.105
What do monarchs eat?

18
00:01:24.106 --> 00:01:28.498
Monarch caterpillars eat milkweed.

19
00:01:28.499 --> 00:01:37.404
Monarch butterflies sip nectar from flowers.

20
00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:40.863
Do monarchs lay eggs?

21
00:01:40.864 --> 00:01:45.700
Butterflies lay eggs on milkweed leaves.

22
00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:49.850
Baby caterpillars hatch from the eggs.

23
00:01:49.851 --> 00:01:55.578
The caterpillars begin eating and growing.

24
00:01:55.579 --> 00:02:00.980
How do the caterpillars become butterflies?

25
00:02:00.981 --> 00:02:04.462
The caterpillars stick to leaves.

26
00:02:04.463 --> 00:02:08.772
Their skin turns into a hard case.

27
00:02:08.773 --> 00:02:16.123
Ten days later butterflies fly out!

28
00:02:16.124 --> 00:02:21.960
Well, it's time to fly away.

29
00:02:21.961 --> 00:02:28.190
Have a safe trip, Monarch Butterfly!
